A message was sent to you regarding record request #26-825:

Good afternoon,



In response to your recent message:



Regarding the message that accompanied the record we provided in response t=
o #8 that said: =E2=80=9CAll responsive records have been provided to you, =
and your request will be closed.=E2=80=9D:

This was an error. There was boilerplate language in the template I was usi=
ng and I neglected to delete the language that was not applicable to this r=
equest. I apologize for the error. Your request is not closed. Your request=
 is currently paused awaiting payment for the email search.



Regarding your request for an explanation of the denial of your fee waiver:

ORS 192.324(5) allows public bodies to =E2=80=9C=E2=80=A6furnish copies wit=
hout charge or at a substantially reduced fee if the custodian determines t=
hat the waiver or reduction of fees is in the public interest because makin=
g the record available primarily benefits the general public.=E2=80=9D Lane=
 County has reviewed your request for a fee waiver and has concluded that t=
he disclosure of the records you have requested would not primarily benefit=
 the general public. Therefore, your request for a fee waiver is denied. Yo=
u may seek review of the County's determination pursuant to ORS 192.401, 19=
2.411, 192.415, 192.418, 192.422, 192.427 and 192.431.&nbsp;



We will keep this request open for 60 days. If we do not receive payment of=
 the invoice within 60 days, we will close this request and you will need t=
o make a new one. ORS 192.329(3)(b).



Sincerely,

Lane County Public Records










